Principle.Description:
The Decomposition Ladder is not a table of contents. Building SP1 forces the
        question "why does this behavior work for the animal" before any technique is chosen;
        skipping it produces technique-shopping instead of diagnosis.

Example.Why:
SP1 explains psychology before any technique; SP2 precedes SP3 with specific
        actionable protocols; SP3 has a named protocol with a measurable progression criterion;
        all terms defined on first use.
